  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 150 PM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nThe upper level trough will move into the region late Sunday into \nMonday departing on Tuesday. This will mean that Sunday and Monday \nwill have more clouds than sunshine as well as showery conditions \nwith occasional thunderstorms. Rainfall totals should be on the \nlighter side with 20% chance or less of 1\" in 24 hours. While soils \nwill have reduced capacity, the anticipation is that lower rates and \namounts will lessen the risk of any short term, flash flooding \nconcerns as well as much impact of on area waterways. With the upper \nlevel trough moving away, drier and brighter conditions may return \nas soon as later Tuesday into Wednesday. However, the pattern looks \nto remain active with the next trough approaching by late Wednesday \nor Thursday with some level of rain and storm chances.",
